<title>LUXEMBOURG: Greece keeps block on EU aid to Turkey.</title>
<headline>Greece keeps block on EU aid to Turkey.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece continued on Tuesday to block 375 million ecus ($424 million) in European Union financial aid to Turkey linked to its customs union with the EU.</p>
<p>Greece continues to block the deal &quot;for the usual reasons&quot;, one EU diplomat said.  </p>
<p>Greece has consistently blocked the aid, citing Ankara's record on human rights and the territorial disputes with its neighbour.</p>
<p>The two countries almost came to war last year over a deserted Greek island in the Aegean.</p>
<p>The aid is intended to help Turkey meet the extra competition created by the customs union which came into effect on January 1, 1996.</p>
<p>In the absence of the aid Turkey complains that it has felt little to no benefit from the deal.</p>
</text>
